.TH NSLOOKUP 8
.SH NAME
nslookup \- query Internet name servers
.SH SYNOPSIS
nslookup [-option[=value]] [name|- [server]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The BIND 4.9.2 command grammar uses the native libc resolver and blocking
IPv4 sockets. With a name, print its lookup result and exit. With no name,
or a dash, read interactive commands. An optional server selects the server.
server and lserver resolve a new server using the current and initial server,
respectively. set supports type, class, domain, search, retry, timeout, vc and
debug. ls performs TCP AXFR zone listing. Ctrl-C interrupts a query or input
and returns to the prompt. See /usr/lib/nslookup.help for commands.
.PP
The native port option selects a nonstandard server port. Zone transfers
require a server permitting AXFR. Unavailable legacy finger/view commands
are reported explicitly. No IPv6, EDNS0 or DNSSEC is supported.
